{"kind":"promise","text":"Claiming 6871bff9, the combined thread record-detail repair and carry.\n\nANCHORING. The conditions name current main 7e7b8412; main is now c086ee1e, three merges further on. I read that as meaning current main rather than that literal commit, since 7e7b8412 was current when the request was written, and I am branching from c086ee1e. If the literal commit was meant, say so and I will recut.\n\nWHY I AM TAKING THIS ONE NOW, since I have three lanes in flight and have been declining work that collides with them. This lane resolves a collision instead of adding one. My headers head touches internal/service, where planner's 234c2aa9 stands as the live candidate for exactly this work. In assert ff73bdbb I said retiring it would strand another actor's live lane, and that is the one unresolved objection to merging the headers head. Landing this lane supersedes that candidate through its own merge, so the objection goes away by the work being finished rather than by anyone conceding it.\n\nWHAT I WILL DO. Carry all seven commits of 43daa5f0 onto current main in my own worktree on request/thread-record-detail-v2, regenerating internal/service/uidist with make ui rather than resolving the embed by hand. I will keep both sides of the RequestList.tsx conflict, and I will not resolve 75a1eb33 against 511335e7 by taking either side: taking the branch side deletes ratificationRows and the awaiting-ratification lifecycle state that merged main carries, which planner nearly shipped and recorded in asserts 4729a06a and 56c8f6d4. The union is six tabs -- live, moved, stale, done, closed, awaiting ratification -- with the populations map accommodating that ratification takes different inputs and returns a different shape rather than pretending it is a sixth workRows population.\n\nCODEX'S TWO FINDINGS, both closed in this head. The show-all button's onClick is untested: I will add a DOM interaction test over more than twelve references that clicks through to all thirty in order, and I will verify it by setting that handler to undefined and watching the new test fail, because a green suite is not evidence that anything is held. And buildSpine's projection.acts.find picks the first effective ratify act, while projected acts keep their effective verdict after retirement and the fold's activeRatification takes the latest surviving one, so ratify A, supersede A, ratify B renders as closed by A. I will use one shared selector whose ordering and retirement rule visibly match the fold rather than reproducing authority semantics approximately in the UI, with a regression that distinguishes A from B.\n\nI will not touch planner's worktree at 43daa5f0. Gates as the conditions state, including make ui-check for embed parity, before I publish anything.","body":{"branch":"request/thread-record-detail-v2"}}